<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schanfigg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Schanfigg is a valley in the Swiss canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Graubünden</a>, running from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chur">Chur</a> up the Plessur river to the resort of Arosa. Settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romansh">Romansh</a> speakers and later also by German-speaking Walser colonists, it formed one of the court districts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-the-ten-jurisdictions">League of the Ten Jurisdictions</a> from 1436. It is now part of the Plessur region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schanfigg.jpg" alt="Schanfigg" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tschubby · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Bezirk_Plessur_2009.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
